; comp_chain -- a compute shader that is deliberately long, and whose
; machine code is different for every specialization of it.
;
; WHAT IT IS FOR. t_vk_pipelines needs many DISTINCT shaders, not many
; copies of one: NVK caches a compiled shader by the hash of its SPIR-V
; plus its specialization, so a hundred pipelines built from identical
; inputs are one compile and one shader-heap upload. A specialization
; constant folded into the arithmetic changes the immediates NAK emits,
; so each pipeline is its own compile, its own cache entry and its own
; allocation out of the shader heap -- which is what makes the heap grow
; past its first 64 KiB chunk and what makes a per-pipeline compile time
; mean anything.
;
; WHY IT IS LONG. A four-instruction shader would measure the driver's
; pipeline-creation overhead and nothing about compiling. 64 blocks of
; seven arithmetic instructions is 448, plus the load, the address
; computation and the store.
;
; WHAT IT COMPUTES, and why none of it folds away:
;
;     acc = gl_GlobalInvocationID.x
;     64 times:
;         acc = acc * 0x9E3779B9 + spec       ; spec is the constant
;         acc = acc ^ (acc >> 13)
;         acc = acc + (acc << 7)
;         acc = acc ^ 0xA5C3F00D
;     out[gl_GlobalInvocationID.x] = acc
;
; Every step depends on the invocation id, so the chain cannot be
; constant-folded however many of its inputs are known; and it is four
; different kinds of operation rather than a repeated multiply-add, so
; there is no closed form for an optimiser to collapse it into. The C
; side of the test recomputes it with the same loop, so a wrong answer
; names the word and the value rather than "the dispatch failed".
;
; GENERATED, MECHANICALLY. The 64 blocks below are the same seven lines
; with the ids renumbered. Reproduce with:
;
;     python3 - <<'EOF' > tests/shaders/comp_chain.spvasm
;     ... the generator recorded in the commit that added this file ...
;     EOF
;
; Do not hand-edit a block: change the generator's template and re-emit,
; or the file stops being the thing it says it is.
;
; SPIR-V 1.3 (--target-env vulkan1.1): StorageBuffer is a core storage
; class from 1.3 on, and before 1.4 OpEntryPoint's interface lists only
; Input and Output variables, which is why the SSBO is not in it.
;
; Copyright (c) mesa-nvk-horizon contributors
; SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
               OpCapability Shader
               OpMemoryModel Logical GLSL450
               OpEntryPoint GLCompute %main "main" %gid
               OpExecutionMode %main LocalSize 64 1 1

               OpDecorate %gid BuiltIn GlobalInvocationId
               OpDecorate %rta ArrayStride 4
               OpMemberDecorate %Buf 0 Offset 0
               OpDecorate %Buf Block
               OpDecorate %ssbo DescriptorSet 0
               OpDecorate %ssbo Binding 0
               OpDecorate %spec SpecId 0

       %void = OpTypeVoid
     %fnvoid = OpTypeFunction %void
       %uint = OpTypeInt 32 0
     %v3uint = OpTypeVector %uint 3
   %ptr_in_v = OpTypePointer Input %v3uint
   %ptr_in_u = OpTypePointer Input %uint
        %gid = OpVariable %ptr_in_v Input

        %rta = OpTypeRuntimeArray %uint
        %Buf = OpTypeStruct %rta
    %ptr_ssb = OpTypePointer StorageBuffer %Buf
       %ssbo = OpVariable %ptr_ssb StorageBuffer
  %ptr_ssb_u = OpTypePointer StorageBuffer %uint

     %uint_0 = OpConstant %uint 0
      %int32 = OpTypeInt 32 1
      %int_0 = OpConstant %int32 0
       %mult = OpConstant %uint 2654435769
       %xorv = OpConstant %uint 2781138957
      %sh_13 = OpConstant %uint 13
       %sh_7 = OpConstant %uint 7

; The specialization constant. Default 1 so an unspecialized pipeline is
; still a valid, different shader rather than a degenerate one.
       %spec = OpSpecConstant %uint 1

       %main = OpFunction %void None %fnvoid
      %entry = OpLabel
      %gidxp = OpAccessChain %ptr_in_u %gid %uint_0
       %gidx = OpLoad %uint %gidxp
